The first Ui times the k and theta.

57:48.720 --> 57:53.960
Yeah, but we have to write it into blocks, right?

57:53.960 --> 58:03.800
So we will have a minus Pw1h, then

58:03.800 --> 58:08.680
we don't multiply anything by m2, so we have a 0.

