59:05.040 --> 59:07.000
All right, so then what we want to solve

59:07.000 --> 59:10.760
is this system of linear equations.

59:10.760 --> 59:12.280
In reality, in general, you never

59:12.280 --> 59:16.640
have equality, because there is always some measuring error.

59:16.640 --> 59:19.400
But in general, you want to build a number of equations

59:19.400 --> 59:25.080
that is large enough to have a system that allows you

59:25.080 --> 59:26.240
for robust calibration.

59:26.240 --> 59:29.560
In particular, we said that with n measurements,

59:29.560 --> 59:32.840
we have a 2n constraints.

59:32.840 --> 59:35.560
So in order to have at least a minimum number of constraints

59:35.560 --> 59:38.120
